==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
TUH (508).png|Bio-Electrokinesis
TFC (166).png|Electrical Telekinesis
TGIS (501).png|Force Field Generation
The More Things Change, Part 2 (489).png|Enhanced Strength
MDGS (677).png|Enhanced Durability
MDGS (664).png|Enhanced Jumping
HIGaDfY (34).png|Enhanced Speed/Quadrupedalism
The More Things Change, Part 2 (528).png|Enhanced Reflexes
The More Things Change, Part 2 (538).png|Electricity Breath
</gallery>
Shocksquatch has the power of electrokinesis, which gives him the ability to manipulate the strong charges of yellow, high-voltage electricity he releases from the bolts on his body, or from his mouth.<ref>''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]''</ref><ref name="TMTCP2">''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]''</ref> It creates electricity via kinetic energy.{{Refn|[[:File:How Shocksquatch Makes Electricity.png]]|group = DR}} These charges can be used to create localized electric fields,{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}} or can be projected as beams at targets a considerable distance away. These beams can even travel across the ground, as demonstrated by [[Crashocker]].<ref>''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref>

Shocksquatch can charge up his body with static electricity, by generating which from his bolts, or by rubbing his hands together, as demostrated by [[Electricyeti]].<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref> Once his body is sufficiently charged, his fur will stand on end, and he can unleash a powerful electric shock to the next thing he touches.<ref name="TMTCP2" /><ref>''[[Many Happy Returns]]''</ref> Shocksquatch can also use this power supportively to beings that are electrically resistant, such as a rolled-up [[Arburian Pelarota (Classic)|Arburian Pelarota]], by transferring his charge to their body.<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref>

By covering objects with his electricity, Shocksquatch can telekinetically move them.<ref name="TFC">''[[The Final Countdown]]''</ref> Shocksquatch can also generate an electric force field that can shoot beams of electricity in multiple directions.<ref name="TGIS" />

Shocksquatch is quite strong, as shown when he punched [[Buglizard (Transformation)|Buglizard]] until the ground fell apart, causing them to fall through into the subway.<ref name="TMTCP2" />

Shocksquatch has a degree of enhanced durability, being able to withstand being flicked off a [[Way Bad]].<ref>''[[The Most Dangerous Game Show]]''</ref> He is also immune to freezing climates thanks to his thick fur.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}}

Shocksquatch is more agile than he looks, as he jumped over Buglizard easily.<ref name="TMTCP2">''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]''</ref>

Shocksquatch is fast enough on foot to keep up with a speeding car,<ref name="S23">''[[Store 23]]''</ref> and can also run on all fours in a similar fashion to a bull or rhinoceros to increase his speed.<ref>''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]''</ref>

Shocksquatch can temporarily shield himself against cosmic radiation by generating electric fields around his body.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}}

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
BiS (518).png|Ineffective Electrokinesis
TTaC (254).png|External Electricity Vulnerability
MaxMonster173.2.png|Electricity Absorption Vulnerability
</gallery>
Shocksquatch's electrokinesis is useless against electricity-impermeable materials, as demonstrated by [[Fistrick]]. He was able to defend himself against the former's attack with his electrically-insulated boots.<ref name="BiS">''[[Bros in Space]]''</ref>

Shocksquatch is helpless while insulated, as he is completely unable to generate electricity, demonstrated by [[Bubble Helmet's Gimlinopithecus Mutation]] when he was insulated by thick foam.<ref name="Outbreak">''[[Outbreak]]''</ref>

Shocksquatch can be harmed by external electricity.<ref name="TTaC">''[[Third Time's a Charm]]''</ref>

Shocksquatch is weak against enemies who can drain electricity, such as [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]].<ref>''[[Max's Monster]]''</ref>

Even though he can resist cosmic radiation, it can still be lethal to Shocksquatch after a certain period of time.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = link}}

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Shocksquatch was accidentally unlocked by [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex Salazar]] after trying to cure Ben and later used by Ben against [[Alpha]] as [[Alpha-Arms]] before he reverted.{{Refn|[[:File:How Shocksquatch Was Unlocked.png]]|group = DR}}

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]'', Shocksquatch defeated [[Buglizard (Transformation)|Buglizard]].
*In ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', Shocksquatch defeated [[Sunder]].
*In ''[[Many Happy Returns]]'', Shocksquatch was defeated by [[Looma Red Wind|Princess Looma]].
*In ''[[Bros in Space]]'', Shocksquatch was defeated and captured by [[Fistrick]] and his [[Muroid]] army.
*In ''[[T.G.I.S.]]'', Shocksquatch shocked a [[Chupacabra]] but was mistaken for a cryptid by [[Secret Saturdays|the Saturdays]] and tackled by [[Fiskerton Saturday|Fiskerton]]. Later, Shocksquatch battled [[V.V. Argost|Argost]] and [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s army of [[Frankencryptid]]s.
*In ''[[Store 23]]'', Shocksquatch stopped the [[Orange Offenders]] from stealing money.
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Shocksquatch defeated [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Ultimate Echo Echo]], but was defeated by Negative [[Ultimate Spidermonkey]].
*In ''[[Max's Monster]]'', Shocksquatch chased after Phil.
*In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', Shocksquatch was defeated by Negative Ultimate Spidermonkey again.
*In ''[[Fight at the Museum]]'', Shocksquatch was defeated by [[Exo-Skull|Exo-Skull]].
*In ''[[Third Time's a Charm]]'', Shocksquatch battled Charmcaster but was teleported out of the library.
*In ''[[The Final Countdown]]'', Shocksquatch fought [[Yetta]] and defeated her off-screen.
*In ''[[The Most Dangerous Game Show]]'', Shocksquatch was defeated by a [[Way Bad]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Shocksquatch appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

